                           "reason":  "Measured against Chromium 153 on Windows: 0.14% of the pixels differ by more than 3 levels of a channel and every box has the same bounding box (flat fills, because Chromium dithers gradients). What is left is the antialiasing along the edge of the turned, rounded box. It covers mix-blend-mode for several modes, with opacity, a translucent source, a radius and a transform, a stacking context that keeps what blends inside it to itself, and background-blend-mode on a colour and on layers. With the blend modes ignored the same fixture measures 29.01%, so it fails.",
